\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Granted is the Saviour's prayer,
\par Sent the gracious Comforter;
\par Promise of our parting Lord,
\par Jesus now to heaven restored.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Christ, who now gone up on high
\par Captive leads captivity;
\par Whiles his foes from Him receive
\par Grace that God with man may live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God, the everlasting God,
\par Makes with mortals His abode;
\par Whom the heavens cannot contain,
\par He vouchsafes to dwell in man.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Never will He thence depart,
\par Inmate of a humble heart ;
\par Carrying on His work within,
\par Striving till He casts out sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. There He helps our feeble moans,
\par Deepens our imperfect groans,
\par Intercedes in silence there,
\par Sighs the unutterable prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Come, divine and peaceful Guest,
\par Enter our devoted breast;
\par Life divine in us renew,
\par Thou the Gift, and Giver too !\tab 
\par                                        Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

